# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package version 2.0.1
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- package-lock.json updated with new dependency tree

### 2. Code Changes

**Modified: src/App.tsx**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the ToastProvider wrapper, after the Suspense block
- Placement ensures analytics tracking works across all routes while maintaining proper React context hierarchy

## Implementation Details

- Followed the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- Used the React/Vite-specific integration method
- Analytics component placed at the root level to track all page views and interactions
- No additional configuration required - analytics will automatically track page views, web vitals, and user interactions

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ Type checking passed with no errors (npm run typecheck)
✅ Linter run (no new errors introduced by our changes)
✅ All dependencies properly installed and lock file updated

## Next Steps for Deployment

1. Ensure Web Analytics is enabled in your Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel (existing or new deployment)
3. Analytics data will automatically start appearing in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Notes

- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- It automatically tracks page views in client-side navigation (React Router)
- No environment variables or additional configuration needed
- Analytics only function when deployed on Vercel (no data collected in local development)
